// G216 (a) U0 (the Position Rows proposal, draft/Proposals/2026-11-03 G216 (a) Position Rows.md §7; U0-design.md in
// artifacts/verify/g216a-oracle): the oracle's representative rows, one per skeleton and composition with the `.None` leaf and its valid
// twin, plus the leaf variants at the bare composition. Each row's verdict is the oracle's, from SPEC 10.5.1, 14.9.2 step 2, 15.6.1 and
// 15.6.4 step 3 (U0-design §1), never dev's: a call judges every Signature position of its instantiated parameter Types under its final
// solution; Result exempts only a position whose sub-Type is a slot the expected result solved; a control-flow argument supplies child
// positions by structure. Skeletons: s1 a named call with caller-fixed Origins (jt1), s2 an Origin the call's solve opens (same9_n),
// s3 the Result position inside a deferred call (q10), s3p the Result layer (mk2, G388), s4 a value call (vc1), s5 a Case construction
// (cx2). Compositions: bare, Tuple, nested Tuple, nested Case, fixed and dynamic arrays, `if`, `match`, a join at an element, a join of
// Tuples, nested joins (scalar and in Tuple elements), a labeled join, `[]`. The unit column names the unit that must pass the row:
// guard (dev passes it; it must keep passing), U2 (the Result layer), U3 (join arguments as rows). Generated by
// artifacts/verify/g216a-oracle/gen-rows.py from the family that ran on dev ddef3be42 (U0-design §6); edit the generator, not the rows.
